                    {
                        "sense_id": "5639ac5f-7c36-3744-b4fc-cfe6741de899",
                        "entry_id": "f80c21d0-284b-3cac-9bc1-b86d270b6775",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Wearing a sunbonnet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "29afb44e-f835-4dc1-8667-d482a2378296",
                                "sense_id": "5639ac5f-7c36-3744-b4fc-cfe6741de899",
                                "text": "While he is at the front end selling calico to some wearisome old lady, sunbonneted and chaffering, a mischievous boy is very apt to be pocketing lumps of sugar for profit, or starting the faucet of a molasses barrel for fun at the other."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4688069c-f4ff-4e92-a99c-dfa070ffa818",
                                "sense_id": "5639ac5f-7c36-3744-b4fc-cfe6741de899",
                                "text": "Standing expectantly on this porch were two fashionably dressed little tots of girls — cut very much on the same pattern, like paper dolls — and a sunbonneted, gingham-clad young woman whose rounded arm lightly held a heavy but spick and span baby, a regular prize winner for plumpness and fairness, a baby of such well-poised deportment that every noddle was kingly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "61deb902-dee2-438e-98d3-c4a9365f0903",
                                "sense_id": "5639ac5f-7c36-3744-b4fc-cfe6741de899",
                                "text": "And there was about her, small and ginghamed and sunbonneted as she was, a certain reserve and dignity and fineness that they resented."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "176d3c88-3b6c-4ac2-ba9e-8272ffd88be6",
                                "sense_id": "5639ac5f-7c36-3744-b4fc-cfe6741de899",
                                "text": "Among them was the “Madonna of the Prairie”—an angelic, idealistic, sunbonneted Euro-American woman, who went west with her family and aided in the Turnerian process of subduing the wilderness."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
